{
  "$comment": [
    "The exact multi-asset symbology and quote vectors: formatter fixtures for equities, sub-cent",
    "crypto, FX and pips, CME decimal futures, 1/32 and 1/4-of-1/32 futures, and variable tick bands,",
    "with reusable quote vectors for last, bid, ask, open, high, low, prevClose, change, changePct,",
    "volume, status, and timestamp.",
    "",
    "One entry per market shape. `format` is the Quick Charts PriceFormat the datafeed resolves;",
    "`prices` are the display cases the one package formatter must produce, each of which must also",
    "parse back to its own value; `quote` carries the raw quote values a board renders for the same",
    "symbol, coherent with one another: change is last minus prevClose on the symbol grid, changePct is",
    "that change over prevClose in percent at two decimals, every price lands on the grid, and the",
    "timestamp is the quote's moment in Unix seconds, the unit the chart's own bars use. `status` is the",
    "datafeed's DataStatus for the symbol. `display` is what the one price formatter writes for each",
    "price field of the quote, change carrying an explicit sign as a board writes it. `board` is the row",
    "the first-party host writes in English through its Watchlist value-formatter port: Last and Chg from",
    "the same price formatter, Chg% as a signed percentage at two decimals, Volume compacted; a case with no",
    "`board` is a punctuation variant of the case before it. Quote values are quote data, never symbology:",
    "they are here as inputs to a display test, not as facts the datafeed's symbology contract owns.",
    "",
    "Read by packages/chart/test/priceFormatter.test.ts and test/inventory/quoteVectors.test.ts. The",
    "private facade's quote work reuses the same file rather than inventing a second set of numbers.",
    "",
    "punctuation: the punctuation the displays below assume. Absent means the default, which is a",
    "'.' decimal sign and no grouping: the chart writes a price ungrouped."
  ],
